<misterromdescription>
    <name>Arlington Horse Racing (v1.40-D)</name>
    <setname>arlingtn</setname>
    <rbf>Gm0rk_ITech8</rbf>
    <mameversion>0289</mameversion>
    <mratimestamp>20261004</mratimestamp>
    <year>1991</year>
    <manufacturer>Strata / Incredible Technologies</manufacturer>
    <category>Sports / Horse Racing</category>
    <players>1</players>
    <joystick>2-way vertical</joystick>
    <rotation>horizontal</rotation>
    <num_buttons>5</num_buttons>
    <buttons names="Win,Place,Show,Collect,Start Race,Coin,Service" default="A,B,X,Y,Start,R,L"/>

    <romstruct>
Board select (ioctl index 1): 1B = itech8 6809 board (3), 64 KB program
(bit 3), program bank bit inverted (bit 4), horizontal; second byte 0A =
2 page large display at 8 MHz (bits 2-1 = 1), YM3812 sound board with a
PIA (bits 4-3 = 1); third byte 05 = Arlington's inputs.
Download stream (ioctl index 0), 1,146,880 bytes:
000000 - 007FFF   32K  sound program                  -> block RAM
008000 - 017FFF   64K  main program                   -> SDRAM bank 0
018000 - 057FFF  256K  OKI samples                    -> SDRAM bank 2
058000 - 117FFF  768K  graphics ROM region (320K used)-> SDRAM bank 1
    </romstruct>

    <rom index="1">
        <part>1B 0A 05</part>
    </rom>

    <rom index="0" zip="arlingtn.zip" md5="9bcc4669c5cd247ccd064fdc5e8aadba">
        <!-- sound program (sound CPU $8000-$FFFF) -->
        <part name="ahr_snd_v1.1_u27.u27" crc="dec57dca"/>
        <!-- main program (64 KB: banks at $4000, last 32 KB at $8000) -->
        <part name="ahr-d_v_1.40_u5.u5" crc="02338ddd"/>
        <!-- OKI M6295 samples -->
        <part name="ahr_srom0.srom0" crc="56087f81"/>
        <!-- graphics ROMs -->
        <part name="ahr_grom0.grom0" crc="5ef57fe5"/>
        <part name="ahr_grom1.grom1" crc="6aca95c0"/>
        <part name="ahr_grom2.grom2" crc="6d6fde1b"/>
        <part repeat="0x70000">00</part>
    </rom>

    <!-- 8 KB battery-backed RAM (CPU $2000-$3FFF) -->
    <nvram index="4" size="8192"/>
</misterromdescription>
